7010 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/P 362 0 R /F 4/M(D:20240623083918+08'00')/HighDpi false/QuadPoints[ 71.8801 623.46 113.65 623.46 71.8801 606.927 113.65 606.927]/Rect[ 71.8801 606.927 113.65 623.46]/T(þÿÿÿ)/Subj(Highlight)/CreationDate(D:20240623082709+08'00')/C[ 0.858824 0.933333 0.956863]/CA 1/NM({5beea765-dbfd-41ed-8483-ae928ffb80dc})/Popup 7011 0 R /AP<</N 7012 0 R >>/Contents(The key to this puzzle is that the first move has to be a check, so when check with the second move, the King won't have the chance to move back to the original square. If you don't check on the first move, then you will have to use your Queen to check on the second move so that it covers the original square and the square the King newly moves to usually the second move has to be a move that Queen makes direct contact with the King.\n\nThe Key is sacrificing the Knight, Qc2!+, the forcing move is Kxe3, then followed by Bg1#.)>>
endobj
