<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/P 367 0 R /F 4/M(D:20240624071820+08'00')/HighDpi false/QuadPoints[ 71.8801 914.82 113.65 914.82 71.8801 898.287 113.65 898.287]/Rect[ 71.8801 898.287 113.65 914.82]/T(þÿÿÿ)/Subj(Highlight)/CreationDate(D:20240624071429+08'00')/C[ 0.717647 0.870588 0.909804]/CA 1/NM({6cf2c494-8aab-479d-a077-230c8548818f})/Popup 7163 0 R /AP<</N 7164 0 R >>/Contents(Moving the Bishop cannot deliver a check, so on the second move, the Queen has to cover both squares, Conclusion is the first move is not a bishop move, A King move is also impossible cause both move can be checked by the Knight. So the first move is a Queen move. it can be either a check or a random move. The answer is Qc5+, followed by either Qd4# or Bf5#.)>>
endobj
