8286 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/P 407 0 R /F 4/M(D:20240629073715+08'00')/HighDpi false/QuadPoints[ 71.8801 914.87 113.65 914.87 71.8801 898.287 113.65 898.287]/Rect[ 71.8801 898.287 113.65 914.87]/T(þÿÿÿ)/Subj(Highlight)/CreationDate(D:20240629073126+08'00')/C[ 0.717647 0.870588 0.909804]/CA 1/NM({45146ae8-d7a7-429a-a0b5-c22ceeb09e00})/Popup 8287 0 R /AP<</N 8288 0 R >>/Contents(We consider that it can't either be a King move or a Knight move, considering the possibility of Kb4 on the second move, Queen will have to cover both c5 and b4 square, only possible move that leads to checkmate is Qc3#, which means both b5 and a4 squares have to be covered by the King and the Rook, it is unlikely to be a Queen move either, cause Queen move will increase the complexity greatly by allowing BIshop and pawn to move on the second move. There are only several possible Knight moves, then we conclude it is Nb7, giving up b4 and b6 squares for King, but can meet both of them with checkmate.)>>
endobj
